<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<UserControl
    x:Class="Winhance.UI.Features.Common.Controls.SettingOutcomeOverlay"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:fluentIcons="using:FluentIcons.WinUI">

    <!--
    The detection-outcome marker that sits INSIDE an input control, for every control that displays a
    value. Placed in the same Grid cell as its control: when the setting is unresolved the control has
    nothing selected and renders an empty content area, and this fills it with the outcome's colour icon
    and text so it reads as the control's own content rather than a marker floating alongside.

    IsHitTestVisible="False" is load-bearing. It suppresses INPUT but never LAYOUT, which gives both
    properties this needs at once:
      * clicks pass straight through, so the control underneath stays fully usable - picking a real
        option is itself the remedy, so covering it would be actively harmful;
      * it is still MEASURED, so a host that stretches its control gets sized by this content. That is
        what stops a ComboBox with no selection collapsing to chevron-width, and it works in every
        language because it measures the real localized string.

    NOTE ON THE TOOLTIP: while pass-through (the default), this element receives no pointer input, so a
    tooltip set HERE can never fire - the same trap as a tooltip on a disabled control. The host puts the
    tooltip on the control the pointer actually hits. The tooltip below is only reachable when a host sets
    IsInteractive="True", which it does when the control underneath is inert anyway.

    Everything it shows comes from the view model's one outcome map, so this, the toggle knob and the
    overview pills can never disagree about what a colour means.
    -->
    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8"
                HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                IsHitTestVisible="{x:Bind IsInteractive, Mode=OneWay}"
                Visibility="{x:Bind OverlayVisibility, Mode=OneWay}"
                ToolTipService.ToolTip="{x:Bind OverlayTooltip, Mode=OneWay}">
        <fluentIcons:FluentIcon Icon="{x:Bind OverlayIcon, Mode=OneWay}" IconVariant="Color"
                                FontSize="16" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
        <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind OverlayText, Mode=OneWay}" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>
    </StackPanel>
</UserControl>
